This page contains no mathematics. It is an archival cover sheet (wrapper) for folio 47a of bundle Math.21. Its contents are:
- the title 'Problem der 8 Königinnen' (the eight queens problem);
- the date '1868 Nov.', thirteen years after Gauss's death in 1855;
- the note '(eingelegt: 48-51)', meaning folios 48-51 are inserted in this wrapper;
- the provenance note '[Geschenk von Frau Listing]', a gift from Mrs. Listing, presumably the wife of J. B. Listing, Gauss's Göttingen colleague. Beneath it is a smaller word, read here as 'Bild', possibly marking the item as a picture or diagram;
- a struck-through shelf mark 'Ma' and a struck-through earlier signature 'Cod. Ms. Gauss Nr. 155 m';
- the pencil remark 'Nicht von Gauss' Hand' (not in Gauss's handwriting).

The material it wraps is shown on the following page. That page has dotted 8×8 grids and the claim that there is only one symmetric solution of the eight queens problem, 'found by Gauss', which yields 8 variants. That enclosed material is a later, non-autograph document about the problem Gauss discussed in his 1850 correspondence with Schumacher. Nothing on this page itself can be reconstructed as a derivation.
